---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About">
  <!-- Static full-bleed background image (sharp) -->
  <div class="fixed inset-0 z-0 overflow-hidden" aria-hidden="true">
    <img
      src="/images/ToddCityOfRocks.jpg"
      alt=""
      class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover object-center"
    />
  </div>
  <!-- Blur only behind the card: clip-path updated by script to match card position -->
  <div id="bio-blur-layer" class="fixed inset-0 z-[1] overflow-hidden pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true" style="clip-path: inset(0 100% 100% 0 round 8px);">
    <img
      src="/images/ToddCityOfRocks.jpg"
      alt=""
      class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover object-center blur scale-105"
    />
  </div>

  <div class="relative z-10">
  <section class="min-h-screen pt-32 pb-24 px-6 md:px-12 max-w-7xl mx-auto">
      
      <!-- Text card (blur shows only behind this area) -->
      <div id="bio-card" class="rounded-lg border border-white/20 shadow-2xl shadow-black/30 bg-black/40">
          <div class="px-6 py-8 md:px-10 md:py-10">
          <h1 class="font-serif text-5xl md:text-6xl mb-4 italic">About Todd</h1>
          <p class="font-mono text-sm text-gray-400 mb-8 font-semibold">Combining Art, Engineering, and Strategy</p>
          <div class="font-mono text-sm text-gray-300 space-y-6 leading-relaxed text-justify">
              <p>
                  Todd Margolis is a product strategist, researcher, and artist who has spent over two decades navigating the "uncomfortable in-betweens" of emerging technology. His career is defined by a unique ability to translate "blue sky" academic inquiry into scalable, market-ready realities. By synthesizing the rigor of computer science with the speculative capacity of new media art, he helps organizations and audiences grasp the layered infrastructures that shape our world.
              </p>

              <h3 class="font-serif text-xl text-white mt-10 mb-4">The Engineering of Experience</h3>
              <p>
                  Todd's trajectory began at the bleeding edge of visualization research. As a grad student and then Visiting Research Programmer at the University of Illinois at Chicago's <strong><a href="/works/uic-evl/" class="text-white underline decoration-white/50 hover:decoration-white">Electronic Visualization Lab (EVL)</a></strong>, he co-invented the <strong><a href="/works/varrier-siggraph/" class="text-white underline decoration-white/50 hover:decoration-white">Varrier™</a></strong> auto-stereoscopic display—a pioneering barrier-strip system that enabled high-resolution Virtual Reality without the need for glasses. This early work in modeling sub-pixel rendering algorithms established the foundation of his practice: removing the friction between the user and the data.
              </p>
              <p>
                  He expanded this expertise as the Technical Director of the <strong><a href ="/works/ucsd-crca/" class="text-white underline decoration-white/50 hover:decoration-white">Center for Research in Computing and the Arts (CRCA)</a></strong> at UCSD. There, he spearheaded the design and architecture of a 10,000 sq. ft. research facility, managing labs dedicated to spatialized audio, motion capture, and <strong><a href ="/works/vroom/" class="text-white underline decoration-white/50 hover:decoration-white">immersive environments</a></strong>. He served as a bridge between diverse disciplines, leading interdisciplinary teams to build "discovery platforms" for massive datasets ranging from <strong><a href ="/works/atlas-in-silico/" class="text-white underline decoration-white/50 hover:decoration-white">metagenomics</a></strong> to <strong><a href ="/works/cultural-analytics/" class="text-white underline decoration-white/50 hover:decoration-white">cultural analytics</a></strong>.
              </p>

              <h3 class="font-serif text-xl text-white mt-10 mb-4">From Telepresence to Product Strategy</h3>
              <p>
                  What distinguishes Todd's approach to product management is his background in high-stakes, real-time media systems. Projects like CineGrid—where he successfully executed the world's first tri-continental premiere of 4K feature-length media via optical networks <strong><a href ="/works/file-4k/" class="text-white underline decoration-white/50 hover:decoration-white">(in 2009)</a></strong> and his work in Telepresence Performance (<strong><a href ="/works/resonations/" class="text-white underline decoration-white/50 hover:decoration-white">ResoNations</a></strong>) required more than just creative vision; they demanded rigorous logistical planning, latency management, and fault-tolerant network architecture.
              </p>
              <p>
                  This experience in Distributed Cinema and networked collaboration directly informs his data-driven approach to product leadership. He views the future of enterprise software not merely as code, but as a collaborative environment where human intuition and agentic logic must coexist.
              </p>

              <h3 class="font-serif text-xl text-white mt-10 mb-4">Applied Research & Innovation Leadership</h3>
              <p>
                  As Sr. Director of Applied Research & Emerging Technologies at <strong><a href ="/works/qlik/" class="text-white underline decoration-white/50 hover:decoration-white">Qlik</a></strong>, Todd accelerated the long-term roadmap for enterprise intelligence. He led a team of machine learning engineers to define the strategy for <strong><a href ="/works/qlik-genai/" class="text-white underline decoration-white/50 hover:decoration-white">Generative AI</a></strong>, moving beyond the hype cycle to develop capabilities that are ethical, scalable, and genuinely useful.
              </p>
              <p>
                  His current artistic focus, <strong><a href ="https://observables.art" class="text-white underline decoration-white/50 hover:decoration-white">Observables</a></strong>, continues this inquiry. Through projects like <strong><a href ="/works/3d-horizons/" class="text-white underline decoration-white/50 hover:decoration-white">Horizons</a></strong> (a stereoscopic intervention into space data) and <strong><a href ="/works/now-and-then/" class="text-white underline decoration-white/50 hover:decoration-white">Now & Then</a></strong> (temporaral astrophotography compositions), he continues to materialize the invisible, proving that the tools of rigorous research and the instruments of artistic expression are one and the same.
              </p>
          </div>
      </div>

  </section>

  <!-- Portrait (after text, before footer) -->
  <section class="px-6 md:px-12 max-w-7xl mx-auto pb-24">
      <div class="max-w-md mx-auto">
          <div class="aspect-[3/4] bg-gray-800 relative overflow-hidden">
              <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-indigo-900/20 mix-blend-overlay z-10"></div>
              <img src="/images/todd.jpeg" alt="Todd Margolis" class="w-full h-full object-cover grayscale hover:grayscale-0 transition-all duration-1000" loading="lazy">
          </div>
      </div>
  </section>
  </div>

  <script>
    function updateBioBlurMask() {
      const card = document.getElementById('bio-card');
      const blurLayer = document.getElementById('bio-blur-layer');
      if (!card || !blurLayer) return;
      const r = card.getBoundingClientRect();
      const radius = 8;
      blurLayer.style.clipPath = `inset(${r.top}px ${window.innerWidth - r.right}px ${window.innerHeight - r.bottom}px ${r.left}px round ${radius}px)`;
    }
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', updateBioBlurMask);
    window.addEventListener('scroll', updateBioBlurMask, { passive: true });
    window.addEventListener('resize', updateBioBlurMask);
  </script>
</Layout>
